# Comando HTML — abrir en Chrome (L2)

Loads on **`/html`** or trigger phrases below. **Complements** `qa-reports-open-chrome.mdc` (auto-open after generate) and L1 `open-links-in-chrome-not-ide.mdc`.

## Triggers

| Language | Phrases |
|----------|---------|
| Slash | `/html`, `html` (as command) |
| ES | `abreme lo que te he pedido en chrome html`, `abre en chrome`, `abre el html`, `muestra el informe en chrome`, `ábrelo en chrome` |
| EN | `open html in chrome`, `open the report in chrome`, `show me the html` |

**Mandatory:** read `.cursor/skills/html/SKILL.md` when triggered.

## Obligation

1. **Resolve** target from argument or conversation context (see skill).
2. **Ensure** `.html` exists — generate twin from `.md` if needed (`documents-md-and-html.mdc`).
3. **Execute** on host (agent runs it):

```bash
google-chrome "file:///absolute/path/to/file.html"
```

Fallbacks: `chromium-browser`, `xdg-open` — same `file://` URL.

4. Reply with absolute path + full `file://` URL + command outcome.

## Prohibited

| Do not | Why |
|--------|-----|
| `browser_navigate` / IDE browser for developer viewing | `open-links-in-chrome-not-ide.mdc` |
| “Recarga / ábrelo tú” without running Chrome | `ai-act-without-asking.mdc` |
| Open `.md` when HTML twin is the presentation target | `/html` means **HTML in Chrome** |
| Truncate `file://` URLs in chat | Developer must copy-paste |

## Scope resolution (summary)

| Input | Action |
|-------|--------|
| Path to `.html` | Open that file |
| Path to `.md` | Open/create `<basename>.html` |
| Basename | Newest match under `.cursor/context/`, `.cursor/QAtest/`, `evidence/`, `documentacion/`, `tmp/` |
| Omitted | Last artifact requested or produced in the chat |

## Close format

```markdown
## Verification
- **Verified:** `test -f <path>`; `google-chrome "file://…"` (exit code)
```

No display → **Not verified:** headless; cite path only.

